    turnFlow: '1. Ante: All players post an equal ante. 2. Deal: Five cards each, one at a time, clockwise. 3. First betting round: Minimum to open is a pair of Kings; players with less must pass; opener may pass. Once someone opens, others may call, raise, or fold. 4. Draw: Starting left of dealer, each player may exchange 0–4 cards (discard face down, receive replacements from stock). 5. Second betting round: Opener (or next active player) may check or bet; others fold, call, or raise. 6. Showdown: Remaining players reveal hands; highest hand wins. If nobody opens, hands are thrown in, pot stays, players ante again and the next dealer deals.',
